- \( \text{NiS} \)  
- \( \text{CuS} \)  
- \( \text{HgS} \)  

The sulfides of these metals are insoluble in acidified solutions. Thus, when \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into the solution, all these sulfides will precipitate.  

The order of precipitation is:  
1. \( \text{HgS} \) (least soluble)  
2. \( \text{MnS} \)  
3. \( \text{FeS} \)  
4. \( \text{NiS} \)  
5. \( \text{CuS} \) (most soluble)  

Thus, \( \text{HgS} \) will precipitate first, followed by \( \text{MnS} \), \( \text{NiS} \), and finally \( \text{CuS} \).  

Final Answer: \(\boxed{\text{All sulfides will precipitate.}}\)
