   \[ 10 \text{ (other)} / 2 = 5 \text{ (lemon)} \]  
3. **Calculate the fraction of students who prefer lemon pie:**  
   \[ \frac{5 \text{ (lemon)}}{40 \text{ total}} = \frac{1}{8} \]  
4. **Convert the fraction to a percentage:**  
   \[ \frac{1}{8} \times 100 = 12\% \]  
5. **Convert the percentage to degrees:**  
