(c) $\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y$<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","(a) $\int_{-1}^{1} 2^{x} d x = \frac{2^x}{\ln 2} \bigg_{-1}^{1} = \frac{2^1}{\ln 2} - \frac{2^{-1}}{\ln 2} = \frac{2 - \frac{1}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{\frac{3}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{3}{2\ln 2}$

(b) $\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+ 2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left(3 e^x + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2}\right) \bigg|_{0}^{1} = \left(3 e^1 + \frac{4}{3} \cdot 1^{3/2}\right) - \left(3 e^0 + \frac{4}{3} \cdot 0^{3/2}\right) = 3 e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 - 0 = 3 e - \frac{5}{3}$

(c) $\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y = \frac{2^{2 y}}{2 \ln 2} \bigg|_{0}^{1} = \frac{2^{2 \cdot 1}}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{2^{2 \cdot 0}}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{4}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{1}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{3}{2 \ln 2}$
