   - The hyperplane \( H \) is defined by the equation \( y \cdot x = 0 \), where \( y \) is a nonzero vector (linear form) and \( x \) is any point in \( \mathbb{R}^n \).

2. **Properties of the hyperplane**:
   - Since \( H \) separates \( b \) from the span of \( a_1, \ldots,a_n \), the span of \( a_1, \ldots,a_n \) lies on one side of \( H \), and \( b \) lies on the other side.
