\[
\nabla f(4, 2, -2) = 2(4) \mathbf{i} + 2(2) \mathbf{i} + 18(-2) \mathbf{i} = 8 \mathbf{i} + 4 \mathbf{i} - 36 \mathbf{i} = 8 \mathbf{i} + 4 \mathbf{i} - 36 \mathbf{i}
\]

The gradient vector \(\nabla f(4, 2, -2)\) is the direction vector of the normal to the surface at \((4, 2, -2)\). The equation of the line passing through \((4, 2, -2)\) and parallel to \(\nabla f(4, 2, -2)\) is:

\[
\begin{cases}
x = 4 + 8t \\
