\[ F = m \cdot a \]  
Given the mass \( m = 30 \, \text{kg} \) and the force \( F = 32 \, \text{N} \), we can solve for the acceleration \( a \):  
\[ a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{32 \, \text{N}}{30 \, \text{kg}} = \frac{16}{15} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  
Thus, the acceleration of the particle is \(\boxed{\frac{16}{15} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).

