In an elastic scattering process where the electron mass is negligible, let the initial and final four-momenta of the electron be \( P_i = (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i) \) and \( P_f = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) \), respectively. Derive an expression for the squared four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \).<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The four-momentum transfer \( S^2 \) is defined as the difference between the initial and final four-momenta:  
\[
S^2 = (P_f - P_i)^2 = (E_f - E_i)^2 - (\mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i)^2.
\]  
The squared four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is the same, but expressed in terms of the energy and momentum components:  
\[
Q^2 = S^2 = (E_f - E_i)^2 - (\mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i)^2.
\]  
