<start_of_turn>model
","To determine the temperature of the diecast component at different times, we use the lumped parameter method, which assumes that the temperature is uniform within the component. The temperature of the component is given by:  
\[
T(t) = T_0 + (T_i - T_0) e^{-t/\tau}
\]  
where:  
- \( T(t) \) is the temperature at time \( t \)  
- \( T_0 \) is the ambient temperature (20°C)  
- \( T_i \) is the initial temperature (345°C)  
- \( \tau \) is the time constant.  

**(i) Temperature after 5 minutes:**  
