\[
\ln k = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT}
\]

The activation energy \( E_a \) is given by:

\[
E_a = \frac{R \ln \left( \frac{k_1}{k_2} \right)}{\frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1}}
\]

Given the rate constants and temperatures:

1. **Convert temperatures to Kelvin:**
   \[
   T_1 = \frac{1}{0.0018 \, \text{K}^{-1}} = 555.56 \, \text{K}
   \]
   \[
   T_2 = \frac{1}{0.0012 \, \text{K}^{-1}} = 833.33 \, \text{K}
   \]

