1. **Oxidation at the anode (anode reaction):**
   \[ \text{Pb} + 2\text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{Pb}_2\text{O}_4 + 2\text{H}^+ + 2e^- \]
2. **Reduction at the cathode (cathode reaction):**
   \[ 2\text{H}_2\text{O} + 2\text{H}^+ + 2e^- \rightarrow 2\text{H}_2\text{O}_2 + 2\text{H}^+ + 2e^- \]
The net reaction is the sum of these two half-reactions, and it results in the formation of lead dioxide (\(\text{Pb}_2\text{O}_4\)) on the anode and hydrogen peroxide (\(\text{H}_2\text{O}_2\)) at the cathode.
